Switch: GXPeekZ on the deko3d NRO (AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D; issue #7, the sun's glare)

GXPeekZ reads depth_peek's latest snapshot, which encoding.cpp fills with a compute pass after the frame's
last EFB pass. The deko3d NRO records its frames through switch/deko/aurora instead of encoding.cpp, so no
snapshot was ever taken: every GXPeekZ read 0 (nearest), and the game drew no sun lens flare or glare (the
sun's five check points never read the sky's 0xFFFFFF), as Dolphin's "Skip EFB access from CPU" does. With
AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D:
- initialize() enables the snapshots without the compute pipeline (Dawn's Null device);
- take_snapshot_request() hands the encoder the pending request (with the 30 Hz limit) and the mapping
  of make_params from logical EFB pixels to the depth image; switch/deko/aurora/dk_encode.cpp copies
  the area around the peeked points with the copy engine after the frame's last pass;
- read_latest() reads the newest copy the GPU has finished (dk::depth_peek_read, no wait).
Without AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D (the Mac) nothing changes.

Switch only (switch/native/aurora/patches); not for upstream.

